    "expert_endorsement_section": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "expert_quote_blk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>\"In over 15 years of guiding backcountry expeditions and facing down brutal weather, the thing that scares me the most isn't apex predators or sheer drop-offs. <strong>It’s the silence.</strong></p><p>Every single year, experienced hikers and everyday families find themselves in life-or-death situations when severe storms hit, wiping out the power grid and severing all communication.</p><p>But you want to know the real tragedy I see when working alongside Search and Rescue? Almost every stranded person we find had a thousand-dollar smartphone and a heavy-duty power bank packed in their bag. They thought they were prepared. But when you're trapped on day three of a freezing, off-grid blackout, lithium batteries drain. Those expensive gadgets just become dead weight. No light. No fire. No way to know what's happening in the outside world.</p><p>Disasters and rolling blackouts don't care about your plans. When total darkness hits and you are completely isolated, you can't pray for a wall outlet. You need the crackle of an emergency weather radio to know when the storm will pass. You need a spark that howling winds can't blow out to start a fire. And you need just enough juice to power up a dead phone and get that one critical SOS text message through.</p><p>Stop trusting your family's safety to a battery that will eventually die. When the grid collapses, <strong>your own two hands should be all you need to generate power, light, and a way out.</strong>\"</p>",
            "alignment": "left",
            "mobile_alignment": "mobile-center",
            "text_size": 14,
            "enable_custom_color": false,
            "custom_text_color": "#ff0000",
            "margin_top": 0,
            "margin_bottom": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "expert_attribution_blk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p></p><p><em><strong>John Hatcher</strong></em></p><p><em><strong>Master Trekking Guide & Survivalist</strong></em></p>",
            "alignment": "left",
            "mobile_alignment": "mobile-center",
            "text_size": 14,
            "enable_custom_color": false,
            "custom_text_color": "#ff0000",
            "margin_top": 0,
            "margin_bottom": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
