    "faq_section": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "How is this different from a standard power bank?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Standard power banks lose their charge over time and become useless when empty. This device features a mechanical hand-crank generator, meaning you can create your own power from scratch, even if the grid has been down for days. </p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Will this fully charge my smartphone?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>No, and it's not meant to. This is designed as an <em>emergency lifeline</em>, not a daily charger. The built-in 1000mAh battery provides a crucial power boost—enough to revive a dead phone to make an emergency 911 call or send text messages when it matters most. </p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Who is this emergency tool designed for?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>It’s essential for campers, hikers, hunters, and anyone living in areas prone to sudden power outages, hurricanes, or severe winter storms. If you want a foolproof backup plan for your family, this belongs in your go-bag.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "How much cranking is required to get power?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>It’s surprisingly efficient. Just 1 to 2 minutes of steady cranking will generate enough power for 5-10 minutes of radio playtime, prolonged flashlight use, or enough battery boost to make a quick, critical phone call. </p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Can I charge it normally before an emergency?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Absolutely. While the hand crank is your off-grid backup, the device features a 5V/1A USB input. You can fully charge its internal battery via a standard wall plug before you head into the woods or when a storm warning is announced. </p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Is it durable enough for harsh conditions?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. Unlike cheap plastic survival gear, this device is encased in heavy-duty aluminum. It’s tough, rugged, and pocket-sized, designed to take a beating while taking up minimal space in your survival kit or glovebox. </p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_7": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "What if it does not feel like the right fit for me?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Your peace of mind is our priority. If you receive the device and don't feel 100% confident in its quality or utility, we offer a hassle-free <strong>[30-Day]</strong> money-back guarantee. Just reach out to our support team. </p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_1",
        "faq_2",
        "faq_3",
        "faq_4",
        "faq_5",
        "faq_6",
        "faq_7"
      ],
